 Ke6 { The result has changed: stepping wide like this lets the opposition slip to his king now. [%cal Rd6e6] }) (3. Kf4 { The f4 square looks natural for your king, but it drops the opposition, and the result changes. } 3... Kf6 4. Ke4 4... Ke6 5. Kd4 5... Kd6 { This square lets him seize the opposition right back from you, and the result changes. [%cal Re6d6] }) (3. Kg2 { The g2 square is tempting, but it drops a row off the opposition battle, and the result changes. } 3... Ke6 4. Kf2 4... Kd5 5. Kf3 5... Kc4 { The result has changed: the opposition needed to stay with your king, not drift away like this. [%cal Rd5c4] }) 1-0


